Package: BARCS
Title: Beta-Binomial Analysis and Regression for CRISPR Pooled Screens
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Hyun-Hwan", "Jeong", , "hyun-hwan.jeong@bcm.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Fits guide-level beta-binomial regression to pooled CRISPR
    screen counts on an arbitrary full-rank design matrix, and tests a
    prespecified coefficient or linear contrast against a Student t
    reference whose degrees of freedom come from independent sequenced
    libraries rather than read depth. Guide counts are modelled against
    unfiltered full-library totals, so a beta-binomial variance separates
    sequencing precision from between-library heterogeneity. Optional
    negative-control calibration and guide-dispersion moderation are
    provided, together with several explicitly labelled guide-to-gene
    summaries. A guide-barcode quantification step maps raw FASTQ reads
    against a library annotation to produce the count matrix. The
    two-group special case and its method are described in Jeong and
    others (2019) <doi:10.1101/gr.245571.118>; the overdispersed
    regression construction follows Baggerly and others (2004)
    <doi:10.1186/1471-2105-5-144>.
